---
import learning from '../data/learning.json';
import HowItWorks from '../components/HowItWorks.astro';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';import {puzzles} from '../data/content.json';
---
<Shell title="Word Groups"><section class="intro"><div class="intro-top"><span class="pill"><span class="dot"></span>{puzzles.length} boards</span></div> <h1>{learning.heading}</h1> <p>Sixteen words, four hidden groups.</p><img class="motif" src="/motif.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="220" height="120" /></section><script is:inline>document.body.setAttribute('data-projector','');</script><section class="panel bottom-gap mode-panel"><div class="panel-body mode-body"><div class="mode-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Mode"><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-daily" class="mode-tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="game">Daily</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-practice" class="mode-tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="game" tabindex="-1">Practice</button></div><div class="mode-head"><h2 id="mode-title">Daily board</h2> <span id="mode-sub" class="muted"></span></div><p id="daily-wait" class="notice" hidden></p><div id="daily-extras" class="daily-extras" hidden><label class="check"><input id="streak-opt" type="checkbox"/> Keep a streak on this device</label><p id="streak-line" class="micro" role="status"></p></div><div id="practice-controls" class="practice-controls" hidden><details class="board-picker"><summary id="picker-summary">Choose a board</summary><p class="micro">A tick and the word “solved” mark boards you have finished on this device.</p><div id="pills" class="pill-grid"></div></details><div class="actions"><label class="check"><input id="remember" type="checkbox"/> Remember this board for 30 days</label> <button class="button secondary" id="new-board">Next board</button> <button class="text-button" id="restart">Restart</button></div></div></div></section><div class="workspace" id="game" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-daily"><section class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><h2 id="board-title">Your connections</h2> <span id="progress" class="pill">0 of 4 groups</span></div> <div class="panel-body"><div id="solved" class="solved-groups"></div> <div id="tiles" class="tiles" role="group" aria-label="Term tiles"></div><p id="feedback" role="status" class="top-gap">Choose four terms, then check the group.</p><div class="actions"><button class="button" id="submit">Check group</button> <button class="button secondary" id="deselect">Deselect</button> <button class="button secondary" id="shuffle">Shuffle</button> <button class="button secondary" id="hint">Show a hint</button> <button class="text-button" id="reveal">Reveal all groups</button> <button class="button secondary no-print" id="print-board" type="button">Print</button></div> <div class="actions top-gap"><span id="stats" class="micro"></span><button class="text-button" id="share">Copy board link</button></div><div id="result-card"></div><div id="session-end"></div><div id="reminder" class="reminder no-print" hidden><h3>Remind me daily</h3><div class="actions"><label class="field reminder-time">Time<input id="remind-time" type="time" value="20:00"/></label><button class="button secondary" id="remind-btn" type="button">Download reminder (.ics)</button></div><p class="micro">This saves a calendar file to your device. Nothing is sent anywhere and no permission is asked.</p></div></div></section> <aside class="sidebar"><HowItWorks><p>Sort sixteen words into four groups of four. Each group you reveal opens a source reading and explains its connection.</p><p>Daily is one board a day, the same for everyone with the same calendar date. It has a limit of four mistakes. The number (#N) changes at midnight in your own time zone, so two people in different time zones can be on different numbers. Practice is always available, with any board and no mistake limit.</p><p>Each group has a tier from 1 (most direct) to 4 (least direct), shown as text when the group is revealed.</p><p>Some words can have more than one connection. Find this board’s intended groups, then inspect the cited readings. When a different connection is also real, the game says so and does not count a mistake.</p><p>“One away” means three selected terms belong to one intended group.</p><p>Stored on this device only, and only if you choose: <code>word-groups:daily</code> (today’s finished board and its result), <code>word-groups:streak</code> and <code>word-groups:streak-opt</code> (your streak, if you turn it on), <code>word-groups:solved</code> (boards you finished) and <code>word-groups:progress</code> (Practice, if you tick Remember). Entries expire after 30 days.</p><a href="/sources/">Source notes ↗</a></HowItWorks></aside></div><section id="explanations" class="top-gap" aria-live="polite"></section><noscript><p class="noscript">The grouping activity requires JavaScript. Source references remain available on the Sources page.</p></noscript><script>import '../lib/app';</script></Shell>
<style>.intro{position:relative}.intro .motif{position:absolute;right:0;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);color:var(--accent);opacity:.55;pointer-events:none}@media(max-width:580px){.intro .motif{display:none}}</style>
